.\" OpenBSD-style concise man page
.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt NL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nl
.Nd number lines of files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl b Ar style
.Op Fl d Ar delim
.Op Fl f Ar style
.Op Fl h Ar style
.Op Fl i Ar number
.Op Fl l Ar number
.Op Fl n Ar format
.Op Fl p
.Op Fl s Ar string
.Op Fl v Ar number
.Op Fl w Ar number
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads lines from the named
.Ar file
or standard input if no file is specified,
and writes them to standard output with line numbers added.
.Pp
Logical pages may be indicated in the input by section delimiters.
A header starts with
.Ql \e:\e:\e: ,
a body with
.Ql \e:\e: ,
and a footer with
.Ql \e: .
Delimiter lines are replaced by empty lines in the output.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b Ar style , Fl Fl body-numbering Ns = Ns Ar style
Set the numbering style for body lines.
The default is
.Cm t .
.It Fl d Ar delim , Fl Fl section-delimiter Ns = Ns Ar delim
Set the section delimiter characters.
If only one character is given, the second defaults to
.Ql \&: .
The default is
.Ql \e: .
.It Fl f Ar style , Fl Fl footer-numbering Ns = Ns Ar style
Set the numbering style for footer lines.
The default is
.Cm n .
.It Fl h Ar style , Fl Fl header-numbering Ns = Ns Ar style
Set the numbering style for header lines.
The default is
.Cm n .
.It Fl i Ar number , Fl Fl line-increment Ns = Ns Ar number
Set the increment between line numbers.
The default is 1.
.It Fl l Ar number , Fl Fl join-blank-lines Ns = Ns Ar number
Consider
.Ar number
consecutive empty lines as one logical line for numbering.
The default is 1.
.It Fl n Ar format , Fl Fl number-format Ns = Ns Ar format
Set the line number output format.
The default is
.Cm rn .
.It Fl p , Fl Fl no-renumber
Do not reset the line number at the start of each logical page.
.It Fl s Ar string , Fl Fl number-separator Ns = Ns Ar string
Set the separator inserted between the line number and the text.
The default is a tab character.
.It Fl v Ar number , Fl Fl starting-line-number Ns = Ns Ar number
Set the initial line number on each logical page.
The default is 1.
.It Fl w Ar number , Fl Fl number-width Ns = Ns Ar number
Set the number of columns used for line numbers.
The default is 6.
.It Fl Fl help
Display help information and exit.
.It Fl V , Fl Fl version
Output version information and exit.
.El
.Pp
The available numbering styles are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm a
Number all lines.
.It Cm t
Number only non-empty lines.
This is the default for body lines.
.It Cm n
Do not number lines.
This is the default for header and footer lines.
.El
.Pp
The available number formats are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm ln
Left justified, no leading zeros.
.It Cm rn
Right justified, no leading zeros.
This is the default.
.It Cm rz
Right justified, with leading zeros.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std nl
.Sh EXAMPLES
Number all non-empty lines of a file:
.Pp
.Dl $ nl file.txt
.Pp
Number all lines including blank lines:
.Pp
.Dl $ nl -b a file.txt
.Pp
Number lines with leading zeros and a custom separator:
.Pp
.Dl $ nl -n rz -s '. ' file.txt
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cat 1 ,
.Xr pr 1 ,
.Xr wc 1
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Nm
utility is compliant with the
.St -p1003.1-2008
specification.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An "vibeutils implementation by Travis Cole"
